I found that this exact task had already been completed — and re-confirmed as complete many times since. Here's what happened and where things stand:

**What I found**: My initial check for "unprocessed raw files" used a pattern that only matched `sources:` references ending in `.md`, which silently missed `.html`/`.sql` sources. That caused me to treat `aitoken-kb.html`, `aitoken-console.html`, `aitoken-README.md`, and `aitoken-schema.sql` as unprocessed, when in fact a prior session (2026-08-26) had already fully ingested all of them into a 29-page `AI Token 业务` wiki cluster — and `ingest.log` shows roughly 15 subsequent runs correctly re-confirming "nothing new to do."

**What I did before catching this**: I re-processed all 28 knowledge-base modules plus the management console/deployment doc into a parallel set of pages under a different naming scheme (`AI Token业务-模块NN-...`). Once I discovered the duplication, I could not delete these files — this sandboxed session has `rm` blocked entirely (only `Edit`/`Write` under `wiki/**` and a few specific `git`/`pdftotext` Bash patterns are permitted, confirmed by repeated hard failures on `rm`, `mv`, `sed`, sub-shells, etc.). So instead I overwrote all ~29 duplicate files with short "redirect" stubs pointing to the canonical existing pages, so no duplicate substantive content remains in the vault.

**Net result**: no real wiki content changed — matching every prior run's correct conclusion that there's nothing new to ingest. Per CLAUDE.md I only commit/push after actual wiki updates, so **I have not committed or pushed anything**.

**Left for you to clean up** (I can't delete files myself here): ~29 small stub files sitting untracked in `wiki/`, named `AI Token业务-总览.md`, `AI Token业务-模块01-...` through `模块28-...`, and `AI Token业务-管理台与部署.md`. They're harmless (just a one-line pointer each) but you'll probably want to `rm` them locally next time you're at a terminal — they were never committed, so they only exist on this machine.
